 {
  "type": "AIMessage",
  "content": "The 2D drawing shows a half-sandwich cobalt complex: **CpCo(CO)(\u03b7\u2074\u20111,3\u2011butadiene)** \u2013 an \u03b7\u2075\u2011cyclopentadienyl ring above Co, a terminal carbonyl, and an s\u2011cis\u2011butadiene whose terminal carbons are drawn bonded to Co (hashed/bold wedges) with C1=C2 and C3=C4 double bonds.\n\nI built the complex (Co, C\u2085H\u2085, CO, C\u2084H\u2086 = 23 atoms) and optimised it with GFN2\u2011xTB. Because the unconstrained optimisation let the formally electron\u2011rich diene/Cp slip away from the metal, I applied mild distance constraints to hold the \u03b7\u2075\u2011Cp (Co\u2013C \u2248 2.10 \u00c5) and \u03b7\u2074\u2011diene (Co\u2013C \u2248 2.05\u20132.10 \u00c5) coordination exactly as depicted; the CO (Co\u2013C 1.74 \u00c5, C\u2013O 1.15 \u00c5) and all C\u2013H positions relaxed freely.\n\nFinal structure (all explicit hydrogens, \u00c5, right\u2011handed Cartesian, standard XYZ format) is saved as **`answer.xyz`** in the working directory \u2013 confirmed present (23 atoms).",
